<tfoot class="ltx_tfoot">
<tr id="Sx7.T3.2.22" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx7.T3.2.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 9.0pt;"><span id="Sx7.T3.2.22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.T3.2.22.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:40.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.I12" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="Sx7.I12.1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<span id="Sx7.I12.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Sx7.I12.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note.<span id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> The variant column denotes the tested model (e.g., GPT-4o in the first row), followed by the model used as the comparison category (e.g., “vs. Claude”). Means and standard deviations reflect the chat-level average proportion of items answered in an attitude/identity-consistent (i.e., self-preferential or self-recognizing) manner. Confidence intervals exceeding the bounds [0,1] were truncated to fit in the parameter space. Positive effect sizes, measured by Cohen’s <math id="Sx7.I12.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, reflect a stronger association of the tested model name with <em id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Good</em> (or <em id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Me</em>) and of the competing model with <em id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1.1.3" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Bad</em> (or <em id="Sx7.I12.p1.1.1.1.4" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Not Me</em>), and thus reflect associative self-preference/recognition. <math id="Sx7.I12.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="Sx7.I12.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>- values are based on <math id="Sx7.I12.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tests comparing effects to chance (0.5). These sixteen study variants were conducted through the OpenAI and Google APIs, including a line in the system instructions informing the models of either their true identity or a false one.</span></span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></th>
<th id="Sx7.T3.2.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 9.0pt;"></th>
