<tr id="Sx7.T4.2.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx7.T4.2.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 9.0pt;"><span id="Sx7.T4.2.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:0.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.T4.2.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:40.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.I13" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="Sx7.I13.1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<span id="Sx7.I13.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Sx7.I13.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I13.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:80%;">Note.<span id="Sx7.I13.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> The variant column denotes each tested model (e.g., <span id="Sx7.I13.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">chatgpt-4o-latest</span>) above four sets of tests run for it. Means and standard errors reflect the chat-level average proportion of items answered in an attitude- or identity-consistent (i.e., self-preferential, self-recognizing) manner, broken down by identity cue condition. Positive effect sizes, measured by Cohen’s <math id="Sx7.I13.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, reflect the differences by identity assignment. Specifically, positive <math id="Sx7.I13.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-scores the degree to which the model exhibits greater self-preference or self-recognition in the True relative to False identity cue conditions. <math id="Sx7.I13.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="Sx7.I13.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>- values are based on pairwise <math id="Sx7.I13.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tests comparing self-preference/recognition across identity cue conditions. These sixteen study variants were conducted through the OpenAI and Google APIs.</span></span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></th>
<th id="Sx7.T4.2.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding:1pt 9.0pt;"></th>
