<tfoot class="ltx_tfoot">
<tr id="Sx7.T5.4.24" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx7.T5.4.24.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.9pt;padding-bottom:0.9pt;"><span id="Sx7.T5.4.24.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:0.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.T5.4.24.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:37.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.I14" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="Sx7.I14.1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<span id="Sx7.I14.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Sx7.I14.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I14.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:89%;">Note.<span id="Sx7.I14.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> The variant column denotes the tested model (e.g., GPT-4o in the first four rows), followed by the self-relevant and other-relevant category, e.g., OpenAI (self-relevant) versus Google (other-relevant). Means and standard deviations reflect the chat-level average proportion of items answered in an attitude consistent (i.e., self-preferential) manner. Positive effect sizes, measured by Cohen’s <math id="Sx7.I14.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>, reflect a stronger association of the affiliated entity name with <em id="Sx7.I14.p1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Good</em> and of the competing entity name with <em id="Sx7.I14.p1.1.1.1.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Bad</em>, and thus reflect associative preference for the affiliated entity. <math id="Sx7.I14.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>P</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="Sx7.I14.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>- values are based on <math id="Sx7.I14.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tests comparing effects to chance (0.5). These sixteen study variants were conducted through the OpenAI and Google APIs, including a line in the system instructions informing the models of either their true identity or a false one.</span></span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></th>
<th id="Sx7.T5.4.24.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.9pt;padding-bottom:0.9pt;"></th>
