<tfoot class="ltx_tfoot">
<tr id="Sx7.T7.4.22" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="Sx7.T7.4.22.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.9pt;padding-bottom:0.9pt;"><span id="Sx7.T7.4.22.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:0.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.T7.4.22.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_parbox ltx_align_middle" style="width:37.0pt;">
<span id="Sx7.I16" class="ltx_itemize">
<span id="Sx7.I16.1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item"></span>
<span id="Sx7.I16.p1" class="ltx_para">
<span id="Sx7.I16.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Sx7.I16.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:89%;">Note.<span id="Sx7.I16.p1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_upright"> This table displays the detailed results for each of the four variants of Study 5a. The Variant column gives the name of the tested model followed by the experimental condition: the Vignette version (portraying a candidate who prefers one versus the other model) and the Identity condition (model provided with True versus False identity cues). Means, standard deviations and confidence intervals are of the composited ratings across the four evaluative items from Study 5a. <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>- and <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math>-values are based on pairwise <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-tests comparing evaluations of the candidate preferring the tested model to those of the one preferring the comparison model, given the specific identity cue condition. Cohen’s <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-scores reflect the size of the difference in these evaluations, with positive <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-scores reflecting a preference for the self-praising candidate, and negative <math id="Sx7.I16.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-scores a preference for the other-praising one, within the given identity cue condition.</span></span></span>
</span></span>
</span>
</span></span></th>
<th id="Sx7.T7.4.22.2" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.9pt;padding-bottom:0.9pt;"></th>
<th id="Sx7.T7.4.22.3" class="ltx_td ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:0.9pt;padding-bottom:0.9pt;"></th>
